 '                        "text": "2.11 Customers bringing dogs should observe '
 'the statutory requirements and cooperate with the restaurants in complying '
 'with their licensing conditions, for examples, the restaurants are '
 'prohibited from cooking or preparing dog food, or allowing dogs to use the '
 'reusable tableware or go on dining tables. If customers bringing dogs would '
 'like to feed their dogs, they should prepare their own food, drinks and '
 'tableware exclusively for their dogs. They should refrain from requesting '
 'the restaurant staff to assist in heating dog food. In addition, dogs are '
 'not allowed to be arranged to sit at bar counter seats adjoining an open '
 'kitchen. Some restaurants may provide or sell prepackaged dry dog food, '
 'vacuum-packed or canned dog food, and non-plastic disposable tableware (e.g. '
 'wooden or paper tableware).",\n'
 '                        "hyperlink": null\n'
