 '                "text": "2.4 The Rabies Regulation (Cap. 421A) stipulates '
 'that dogs must be vaccinated against rabies, microchipped and licensed. '
 'Customers bringing dogs must ensure that their dogs meet the requirements '
 'under the Rabies Ordinance. They should also understand that restaurants may '
 'request them to produce the licences of their dogs for verification. If a '
 'diner fails to produce the relevant licence, the restaurant has the right to '
 'refuse entry of the dog.",\n'
