 '                        "text": "1.5 For effective control of their dogs, '
 'each adult diner should not bring more than two dogs. Restaurant operators '
 'may set an upper limit on the total number of dogs admitted to the premises '
 'at any one time according to the actual conditions of the premises, such as '
 'area, seating spacing, customer flow and the main types of dishes served '
 '(e.g. refreshments or congee).",\n'
