 '                "orig": "Q12: Under the licensing conditions, restaurants '
 'are prohibited from heating food at the table. However, if electric heating '
 'or small heating devices such as alcohol burners are used instead of '
 'traditional gas stoves, would such methods be exempt from this restriction? '
 'Are there any exceptions?",\n'
 '                "text": "Q12: Under the licensing conditions, restaurants '
 'are prohibited from heating food at the table. However, if electric heating '
 'or small heating devices such as alcohol burners are used instead of '
 'traditional gas stoves, would such methods be exempt from this restriction? '
 'Are there any exceptions?",\n'
 '                "formatting": null,\n'
 '                "hyperlink": null\n'
