 '                ],\n'
 '                "orig": "The FEHD has stipulated in its licensing conditions '
 'that if a dog causes injury to any person on the premises and the matter is '
 'reported to the police, the licensee must report the case to the FEHD using '
 'the designated form within two working days of the occurrence. Restaurant '
 'operators may also refer to the coming \\"Guideline on Good Practices and '
 'Behaviour\\" to formulate response plans, which include measures such as '
 'consoling affected customers and reminding dog owners of their legal '
 'responsibilities.",\n'
 '                "text": "The FEHD has stipulated in its licensing conditions '
