 '                        "text": "1.38 In the event that a dog barks '
 'persistently, stares at people, exhibits aggressive behaviour, or causes '
 'nuisance to other diners, restaurant operators should, when it is safe to do '
 'so, ask the customer with the dog to take appropriate control measures, '
 'including temporarily removing the dog from the premises. The provision of '
 'takeaway packaging services may be considered to assist diners who need to '
 'leave early in taking their unfinished meals away.",\n'
