 '                        "text": "1.40 The Rabies Ordinance (Cap. 421) sets '
 'out the arrangements for handling bites by animals (including dogs). The '
 'restaurant operator should remind the customer with the dog concerned to '
 'report the incident to the Police. If necessary, the restaurant operator may '
 'also proactively contact the Police and should promptly notify its insurance '
 'company to handle the related legal and claims matters. With the consent of '
 'the parties involved, the contact information of the customer with the dog '
 'concerned and the injured person may be recorded for future follow-up.",\n'
 '                        "hyperlink": null\n'
