 '                "text": "1.34 If the premises are more crowded during peak '
 'hours (such as lunch and dinner rushes), restaurant operators may consider '
 'suspending seating new customers bringing dogs, and reminding customers with '
 'dogs to prevent their dogs from lingering in or lying across main '
 'passageways and to shorten the leashes, so as to ensure that the movement of '
 'people and the serving of food and drinks within the premises are not '
 'obstructed. Where customers bringing dogs need to wait for seats, restaurant '
 'operators should consider providing a service to notify customers when seats '
 'become available, so as to avoid inconvenience to customers without dogs and '
 'other passers-by due to the gathering of customers with dogs waiting outside '
 'the restaurants.",\n'
