 'actual circumstances, decide whether to designate dog-friendly zones. If '
 'they decide to do so, the provision of physical barriers (e.g. gates or '
 'hoardings) is advisable to prevent dogs from entering other areas. If '
 'permission for an outside seating accommodation (OSA) has already been '
 'granted, priority may be accorded to designating the OSA, which is more '
 'ventilated and usually more open, as a dog-friendly zone, and shade '
 'facilities may also be provided as needed.",\n'
